WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.699
When every element is equally loud, the viewer
must decide where to begin.

2
00:00:04.699 --> 00:00:08.298
Visual hierarchy makes that decision
intentional.

3
00:00:08.298 --> 00:00:13.167
One element becomes the entry point,
supporting information follows, and details

4
00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:15.196
settle into a readable order.

5
00:00:15.196 --> 00:00:19.525
The design is not merely decorated; attention
is being organized.

6
00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:23.739
A larger headline is one hierarchy cue, but
not the only one.

7
00:00:23.739 --> 00:00:29.086
Weight, color, position, spacing, and
alignment also shape what appears primary

8
00:00:29.086 --> 00:00:29.977
or secondary.

9
00:00:29.977 --> 00:00:33.854
Strong hierarchy uses a few coordinated
differences.

10
00:00:33.854 --> 00:00:38.132
Random changes create noise; consistent
differences create relationships

11
00:00:38.132 --> 00:00:43.123
that readers can learn quickly. To test a
layout, look away and return for one

12
00:00:43.123 --> 00:00:46.242
second. What do you notice first, second, and
third?

13
00:00:46.242 --> 00:00:50.950
If that order does not match the message,
adjust the system rather than adding

14
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:51.891
more emphasis everywhere.

15
00:00:51.891 --> 00:00:57.054
A successful hierarchy makes the important
path feel natural while leaving the

16
00:00:57.054 --> 00:00:58.245
supporting material available.
